# Semicolons and commas are distinct separators with their own node types:
# `;` is a lower-precedence (prec 1) separator that prints as `;`, while `,` is
# a higher-precedence (prec 3) list separator that prints as `,`. They must not
# collapse into each other.
A; B, C

# Mixed across precedence levels within one expression.
First, Second; Third, Fourth

# Trailing separators of each kind.
1, 2,
X; Y;
